    "intro_html":  "Jalfrezi started as a way to use up leftover roast meat, stir fried with onions and peppers so it came back to life instead of getting thrown out. That origin story is why it is the driest of the Indian curries, more stir fry than stew, with peppers that still have snap in them. Dry curries hold their texture in a container far better than saucy ones do. Each bowl runs {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
